        "name": "Arduino UNO R3",
        "refPrefix": "A",
        "controller": true,
        "doc": {
          "title": "Arduino UNO R3 (SKU A000066): product reference manual section 5 Connector Pinouts (5.1 JANALOG, 5.2 JDIGITAL), and the Full Pinout PDF (pages 1, 3 and 4)",
          "url": "https://docs.arduino.cc/resources/datasheets/A000066-datasheet.pdf",
          "url2": "https://docs.arduino.cc/resources/pinouts/A000066-full-pinout.pdf",
          "revision": "UNO R3 (A000066); datasheet footer 'Modified: 21/10/2026'; full pinout 'Last update: 6 Oct, 2022'",
          "retrieved": "2026-10-23",
          "pinNumbering": "JA-n is pin n of connector JANALOG (power header then analog header, 14 pins) and JD-n pin n of JDIGITAL (18 pins), as numbered in the datasheet tables. ICSP-n and ICSP1-n are the 6-pin ICSP headers of the ATmega328P and the ATmega16U2, numbered as on pinout page 4.",
          "notes": "The datasheet lists JDIGITAL 17 and 18 as 'A4/SD4' and 'A5/SD5' ('Analog input 4/I2C Data line (duplicated)'); the pinout labels them D18/SDA and D19/SCL, so each is grouped with A4 or A5. IOREF is 'connected to 5V' (datasheet), so it shares group 5V with +5V and ICSP-2. GND pins JA-6, JA-7, JD-15, ICSP-6 and ICSP1-6 form group GND; ICSP1-2 is also +5V. ICSP-1/3/4 are the ATmega328P's CIPO/SCK/COPI (D12/D13/D11) and ICSP-5 its RESET, so they are grouped with those header pins. ICSP1-1/3/4/5 belong to the ATmega16U2 USB bridge and are not connected to the user headers. Digital numbers D14-D19 of the analog pins are aliases on A0-A5. The pinout notes that CIPO/COPI were previously called MISO/MOSI; both names are aliases. Roles: +5V, +3V3 and IOREF power_out (board regulator outputs), VIN power_in."
        },
